profile: runtime-mirust.next-recursive-prompt.v43
updated_utc: 2026-07-22T12:11:11Z
prompt: >
  Continue only in E:\Source\Rust\TinyRustLM.com as tinyrustlm-agent. Begin with wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-exact-flat-named-target-performance-memory-2026-07-22.md, its immutable observation and child receipt, the browser-WASM and exact-flat foundation reports, .uai/test-plan.uai, and the two active Improvement assignments. Preserve every scalar, exact-flat, browser, physical-target, and failure receipt. Never rerun any browser or physical-target `--write` command. Named-host latency, throughput, and process memory are verified only for the registered workloads; energy and independent chassis attestation remain false. The next executable retrieval slice is a sealed representative corpus with exact ground truth and recall/MRR/NDCG/usefulness gates plus crash-recovered durable deletion and compaction proof. Only after those baseline gates pass may a source-pinned compressed arm be preregistered at equal effective bytes. Keep static weights, KV cache, and durable indexes separate. Claim no TurboVec parity, compression, broad performance, representative quality, product integration, live MemoryEndpoints, outside P2P, catalog, or release completion from local experiment evidence.
primary_goal: >
  Advance the exact f32 baseline from verified browser and named-host measurements into trustworthy comparison evidence without product integration: evaluate a sealed corpus, prove crash-recovered durable deletion, then compare one independently pinned compressed arm under preregistered equal-byte gates.
