active_intake_truth: >
  These are outbound assignments awaiting independent reports. Keep them active. They prove no contract, algorithm, quality, performance, compatibility, live account, or deployment fact.
engineering_rules:
  - TinyRustLM is pre-release; incur no technical debt and provide no legacy or backward-compatibility support.
  - Rewrite cleanly and remove superseded implementation after verification; preserve immutable receipts as audit evidence only.
  - Keep third-party review downloads outside every repository and Git under E:\Source\external\{project-name}.
  - Do not modify receipt-bound exact-flat inputs without creating a new preregistration and child receipt identity.
  - Keep experiment code publish-disabled, dependency-free, unsafe-free, and absent from product imports until all promotion gates pass.
  - Preserve raw failures, fixed seeds, exact identities, bounded allocations, untouched outputs, and current zero-live campaign counters.
  - Never train unresolved 42-record or 668-record human-review data.
next_steps:
  - Build a sealed, provenance-bound retrieval corpus with exact ground truth, filters, ties, drift, deletion, restart, and privacy cases.
  - Add crash/power-loss persistence tests with same-directory atomic promotion and post-compaction byte-level deletion evidence.
  - Record energy and independent physical-chassis attestation only from a separately authorized measurement source; never infer either from the current host probe.
  - Pin one compressed retrieval method by exact source and license identity, then freeze an equal-effective-byte comparison before implementation.
success_criteria:
  - Exact-flat receipt history remains immutable and validators pass against unchanged bound inputs.
  - Existing real-browser and named-target receipts retain exact bytes, toolchains, hardware, settings, seeds, raw failures, and bounded authority.
  - Corpus metrics are computed against sealed exact ground truth with no result-driven threshold changes.
  - Durable deletion is proved after crash recovery and compaction, not inferred from in-memory tombstones.
  - No product, TurboVec, compression, performance, MemoryEndpoints, P2P, catalog, or release claim exceeds its receipt evidence.
